<title>UK: Allied retailing details expansion plans.</title>
<headline>Allied retailing details expansion plans.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drinks group Allied Domecq Plc said on Wednesday that its retailing division was launching a 150 million pound ($253.1 million) investment programme, which would create 4,000 full and part-time jobs over the next 12 months.</p>
<p>It said that the investment programme would focus on the expansion of the company's three market leading brands - Big Steak Pub with Wacky Warehouse, Firkin and Mr Qs.</p>
<p>Allied Domecq Retailing, which operates 3,900 managed and leased pubs, said there would be more than 140 developments as part of the programme, including a number of acquisitions. ($ = 0.592 British Pounds)</p>
</text>
